.TH UNIM-SETTINGS 1 "May 2026" "UNIM 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-settings \- UNIM settings dialog (GTK4 + libadwaita)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-settings
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBunim\-settings\fR is the dedicated settings dialog for UNIM (Universal
Next\-generation Input Method). It is a GTK4 + libadwaita window that
edits the same configuration file the daemon reads
(\fI~/.config/unim/config.yaml\fR), with every change synced live to the
running daemon over D\-Bus.
.PP
In UNIM 0.3.0 this dialog replaces the previous \fBunim\-gui\-gtk\fR and
\fBunim\-gui\-qt\fR binaries. The Qt6 dialog (\fBunim\-gui\-qt\fR) has been
retired \(em \fBunim\-settings\fR is now the single GUI for all desktops.
.PP
The dialog is normally launched from the tray indicator (\fBunim\-indicator\fR)
or by typing its name in a launcher.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SETTINGS GROUPS
.TP
.B Layouts and Keymap
Korean layout selection (10 built\-ins + user layouts under
\fI~/.config/unim/layouts/*.json\fR), keystroke profile editor.
.TP
.B Moachigi (Chord input)
\fBchord_window_ms\fR slider (0\(en200 ms, default 60 ms), bidirectional
combine toggle. See FAQ Q18 for recommended values.
.TP
.B AutoTypeFix
Forward/reverse Korean\-English typo correction, learning blacklist
management, per\-application mode share.
.TP
.B Popup behaviour
Hanja popup compact/expanded toggle, special character popup, emoji
popup. Popup rendering itself is owned by \fBunim\-popup\-service\fR.
.SH D\-BUS INTERFACE
.TP
.B Daemon service
org.atit.unim.Daemon
.PP
The dialog reads and writes configuration via \fBGetConfig\fR / \fBSetConfig\fR
methods on the daemon. It does not expose its own D\-Bus service \(em it is
a pure client.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UNIM_DEVELOP
Set to "1" to enable verbose debug logging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
User configuration file (single source of truth).
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/layouts/*.json
User\-defined layout profiles (loaded automatically by the daemon).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-daemon (1),
.BR unim\-cli (1),
.BR unim\-indicator (1),
.BR unim\-popup\-service (1)
